    Bug 2001549 - Remove race conditions in MsgOperationObserver. r=mkmelin


    The failing test revealed the following issues:

    1. The listener for the `compose-prepare-message-failure` event is not removed
       for successful save operations. A follow-up save operation is adding an
       additional listener, which can cause multiple calls in case of later errors.
       This is solved by using the same event for both cases (success and failure).

    2. In MV3 extensions, the background can be terminated after inactivity. If that
       happens in `MsgOperationObserver.waitForOperationAndHandleResults()` during a
       message operation, after `onConvertSync()` was called, but before the `onSuccess()`
       or `onFailure()` callbacks are called, the listeners are removed and re-added.
       This throws away stored converted data on the removed listeners. The mentioned
       callbacks will then fail, since they do not find the data. This is solved by
       attaching the data directly to the `MsgOperationObserver` instance. We can also
       shortcut the data conversion, since multiple listeners registered for the same
       extension will get the same event data, and the `onConvertSync()` only needs to
       be called once.

    3. We used `Promise.all()` for waiting for the preparation task and the delivery
       task to complete. A failure in the delivery task, before the preparation task
       has finished, may skip calling `onConvertSync()`. The `onFailure()` callback
       will then not find the required data and fail with the error thrown in the test.
       This is solved by explicitly waiting for the preparation task first. I did
       not encounter situations where the preparation task failed to resolve.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D273769

